<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: HORSE RACING-IRISH DERBY RESULT.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-IRISH DERBY RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-06-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Result of the Group One Irish</p>
<p>Derby for three-year-olds, run over one and a half miles (2.4</p>
<p>kms) at The Curragh on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Desert King 11-2 (ridden by Christy Roche)</p>
<p>2. Dr Johnson 12-1 (Johnny Murtagh)</p>
<p>3. Loup Sauvage 8-1 (Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p>Ten ran. Silver Patriarch 5-4 favourite</p>
<p>Distances: One length, short head</p>
<p>Winner owned by Michael Tabor and trained in Ireland by</p>
<p>Aidan O'Brien.</p>
<p>Value to winning owner: 398,200 pounds ($662,000)</p>
